{
  "name": "Particle Storm",
  "description": "Half a million particles simulated in a Feedback texture and drawn by a Render 3D node as additive point sprites in one draw call: a vortex with an updraft, curl turbulence, respawning particles coloured by speed, bloom. Reacts to music. Parameters: Storm, Look, Music.",
  "version": "1.0",
  "timestamp": "2026-10-25T20:19:43.421Z",
  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -118,
        "data": {
          "text": "# Particle Storm\nHalf a million particles simulated in one rgba32f Feedback and drawn by a Render 3D node as additive point sprites (one gl.POINTS draw: no vertex buffer, the vertex id is the particle). A vortex with an updraft, curl turbulence and respawning particles; colour by speed.\n- Parameters (P): Storm, Look, Music.",
          "width": 420,
          "height": 150,
          "color": "yellow"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -68,
        "data": {
          "text": "## Storm sim\nFeedback 1024 x 1024 rgba32f: rows 0-511 positions (w = life), rows 512-1023 velocities (Instance Data, blocks = 2) = 524,288 particles.",
          "width": 300,
          "height": 100,
          "color": "blue"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -88,
        "data": {
          "text": "## Particles\nInstance Data reads each particle's position and velocity; Make Instance places it and colours it by speed. The material draws a soft round sprite (Surface.uv = gl_PointCoord) with additive blending. Particles = Mesh.count (live).",
          "width": 320,
          "height": 120,
          "color": "violet"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 3,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -48,
        "data": {
          "text": "## Post\nBright pass into a small Feedback, bloom, vignette.",
          "width": 260,
          "height": 80,
          "color": "orange"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 4,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 80,
        "y": -68,
        "data": {
          "text": "## Music\ndrive = music x smoothstep(0.02, 0.12, level) speeds up and stirs the storm; beat pulses flare the particles and the bloom: Beat (clock stable, gate fade) pulse x confidence, so they come from the stable beat clock and fade out while it is unsure (a track change: it holds the old tempo, then glides to the new one) and with the audio off.",
          "width": 300,
          "height": 100,
          "color": "pink"
        }
      },
